<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32954" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκτᾰρ-άσσω</span></b> , 
			Att.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκτά̆ρ-ττω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>throw into confusion,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς ἵππους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ascl.
					<u>Tact.</u>
					7.4
				</span></i>
			, etc.; <i>agitate,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν δῆμον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Cor.</u>
					19
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Or.</u>
				2.97d
			</span></i> :—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be greatly troubled, be confounded,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπό τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					15.5
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				12.552f
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Somn.</u>
					16
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in 
				Pass.
			 also, <i>to have a bowel-complaint,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοιλίη ἐκταραχθεῖσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Aph.</u>
					4.60
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Epid.</u>
				1.15
			</span></i>.</div>
